{"name":"Pineapple Wine","hex":"#dbbc6c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pineapple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tropical plant, Ananas comosus, native to South America, having thirty or more long, spined and pointed leaves surrounding a thick stem.","The ovoid fruit of the pineapple plant, which has very sweet white or yellow flesh, a tough, spiky shell and a tough, fibrous core."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["A common safeword."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pineapple"},{"term":"wine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting grape juice, with an ABV ranging from 5.5–16%.","An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting other substances, producing a similar ABV."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To entertain (someone) with wine.","To drink wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fruit wine","blocks":[{"text":"Fruit wines are fermented alcoholic beverages made from a variety of base ingredients ; they may also have additional flavors taken from fruits, flowers, and herbs. This definition is sometimes broadened to include any alcoholic fermented beverage except beer. For historical reasons, cider and perry are also excluded from the definition of fruit wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/%D5%86%D5%BC%D5%A1%D5%B6_%D5%A3%D5%AB%D5%B6%D5%AB.jpg/330px-%D5%86%D5%BC%D5%A1%D5%B6_%D5%A3%D5%AB%D5%B6%D5%AB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit_wine","wikidata":"Q633625"},{"title":"Pineapple","blocks":[{"text":"The pineapple is a tropical plant with an edible fruit; it is the most economically significant plant in the family Bromeliaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/%E0%B4%95%E0%B5%88%E0%B4%A4%E0%B4%9A%E0%B5%8D%E0%B4%9A%E0%B4%95%E0%B5%8D%E0%B4%95.jpg/330px-%E0%B4%95